It does *not* compare artifacts.

> > This for example, weapon.c function select_hwep()
>
> > 	/* prefer artifacts to everything else */
> > 	for(otmp=mtmp->minvent; otmp; otmp = otmp->nobj) {
> > 		if (otmp->oclass == WEAPON_CLASS
> > 			&& otmp->oartifact && touch_artifact(otmp,mtmp)
> > 			&& ((strong && !wearing_shield)
> > 			    || !objects[otmp->otyp].oc_bimanual))
> > 		    return otmp;
> > 	}

What it does is select the first one the loop encounters.

> Note the for loop there: that looks through the monster's inventory in
> order. When a monster picks up an item, it gets inserted at the front
> of the minvent chain (add_to_minv(): "/* else insert; don't bother
> forcing it to end of chain */"), so newer items are reached (and, if
> satisfactory artifacts, selected) first.

And based on the nature of how items go into a monster's
inventory that means they will always select to most
recently picked up artifact.

> > This is sufficiently annoying for me to complain that it is a bug.
>
> It's certainly not a bug; it's working as designed. It may or may not
> be a misfeature.

I thought about this for quite some time before I decided that
I agree with it as designed.

Let's say your pet is now wielding Frost Brand.  You are stuck
with Orgesmasher.  You can take Frosty from your pet without
losing the pet by dropping Ogresmasher.  You pet will pick it
up, switch and drop Frosty.

Now consider that you already have Greyswandir and that just
happened by accident.  You really wanted some other pet to take
Ogresmasher but the most powerfull pet got there first.  You
can *still* drop Frosty again.  The same pet will pick it up
all over again, and since it's now at the front of the inventory
switch to it and drop Ogresmasher.  Then you can manuever your
number two pet closer, drop Ogresmasher and try again.

Having multiple pets means they do compete with each other for
stuff you drop.  This is a system that can use patience to give
each pet the exact artifact you want.  If pets did the order
based selection the first one to pick up Frosty would never let
it go for anything but Snickersnee, Stormy or the ToM.  You
would need to use a whip (that should reduce tameness!) or kill
your pet to retrieve your best artifacts where as it is
designed you can hand them a junk artifact and trade.  "My
master said this is the one I should use.  In loyalty I will do
as asked."


